        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:12 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Attorney General John D. Ashcroft)",
      "case_id": "2003-03-218",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b8d232e818eb83f1b7f9561faaba84b4dbdc49b0bae71620df32313cf53e1bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b8d232e818e-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Child Online Protection Act addresses a problem that all three branches of our national Government have repeatedly and consistently described as compelling, the pervasive and essentially unavoidable commercial Internet pornography that inflicts substantial physical and psychological damage on our children."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2003-03-218",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b8d232e818eb83f1b7f9561faaba84b4dbdc49b0bae71620df32313cf53e1bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b8d232e818e-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Mr. Olson, part of the problem is that the pornography laws that would apply to adult viewers don't seem to be enforced very well, the obscenity laws."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2003-03-218",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b8d232e818eb83f1b7f9561faaba84b4dbdc49b0bae71620df32313cf53e1bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b8d232e818e-0000-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The magnitude -- we point this out on page 20 of our brief -- that 11 million children visit these porn sites every week, and that between the ages of 15 and 17, 70 percent of the children, according to the statistics that we cite, visited porn site inadvertently."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2003-03-218",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "6b8d232e818eb83f1b7f9561faaba84b4dbdc49b0bae71620df32313cf53e1bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b8d232e818e-0000-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "has agreed is a compelling problem."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2003-03-218",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b8d232e818eb83f1b7f9561faaba84b4dbdc49b0bae71620df32313cf53e1bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b8d232e818e-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Mr. Olson, may I ask you a question about the -- on the -- the meaning of this very provision?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2003-03-218",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b8d232e818eb83f1b7f9561faaba84b4dbdc49b0bae71620df32313cf53e1bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b8d232e818e-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Well, they're making money out of the sale of -- of the product, which itself is not pornographic."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2003-03-218",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b8d232e818eb83f1b7f9561faaba84b4dbdc49b0bae71620df32313cf53e1bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b8d232e818e-0001-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yes, I believe they would, Justice Stevens, that if the idea is to sell -- to use the material that fits the definition, I keep saying the word pornography because I want to use the shorthand, and that is to make commercial use of it by making money out of it, whether they sell -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2003-03-218",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b8d232e818eb83f1b7f9561faaba84b4dbdc49b0bae71620df32313cf53e1bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b8d232e818e-0001-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress would not have wanted to create that massive loophole, because the people that are -- this is a multi-billion dollar business, the people that are doing it would readily adapt to that type of a loophole."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2003-03-218",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b8d232e818eb83f1b7f9561faaba84b4dbdc49b0bae71620df32313cf53e1bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b8d232e818e-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The point is that the serious value for minors clause does not protect as much material as the serious value for adults clause in the obscenity statute. That by definition must be true, and in fact, as a society, just even using common sense -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2003-03-218",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b8d232e818eb83f1b7f9561faaba84b4dbdc49b0bae71620df32313cf53e1bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b8d232e818e-0001-0007",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The burden here is much greater because the quantity and diversity of speech affected is much greater and the number of users affected is greater."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2003-03-218",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b8d232e818eb83f1b7f9561faaba84b4dbdc49b0bae71620df32313cf53e1bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b8d232e818e-0002-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "that's the only kind of a statute this Court has upheld. That's the -- that's what they upheld in Ginsberg is that you can make it a crime to deliberately sell this material to the child."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice (unspecified)",
      "case_id": "2003-03-218",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b8d232e818eb83f1b7f9561faaba84b4dbdc49b0bae71620df32313cf53e1bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b8d232e818e-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: All right. Suppose -- what in your opinion is the right way for Congress to go about this?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Theodore B. Olson",
      "case_id": "2003-03-218",
      "confidence": 1.0,
